Based on the standalone [Resource example](xcsh://terraform-documentation/documentation/resources/rate_limiter/examples/resource/index.md?view=context#resource), using only your supplied resource values:

```hcl
terraform {
  required_version = ">= 1.14"

  required_providers {
    xcsh = {
      source  = "f5-sales-demo/xcsh"
      version = "= 12.4.0"
    }
  }
}

provider "xcsh" {}

resource "xcsh_rate_limiter" "synthetic_rate" {
  name      = "synthetic-rate"
  namespace = "synthetic-lab"
}
```

**Provider requirements:** Pinned to bundled provider **v12.4.0**. Terraform ≥1.14 follows the maintained [provider requirements](xcsh://terraform-documentation/documentation/provider/setup/index.md?view=context), superseding the example’s older ≥1.0 declaration. Supply authentication and `XCSH_API_URL` through environment variables.

**Supplied field constraints:**

| Field | Provider schema | Documented upstream constraints |
|---|---|---|
| [`name`](xcsh://terraform-documentation/documentation/resources/rate_limiter/properties/index.md?view=context#schema-name) | Required string; `NameValidator()` | Unique within namespace; immutable through replace API; 1–63 characters; pattern below |
| [`namespace`](xcsh://terraform-documentation/documentation/resources/rate_limiter/properties/index.md?view=context#schema-namespace) | Required string; `NamespaceValidator()` | DNS label; 1–63 characters; pattern below |

Both fields’ upstream pattern is `^[a-z]([-a-z0-9]*[a-z0-9])?$`: lowercase-letter start, lowercase letters/digits/hyphens, alphanumeric end. Both supplied values satisfy it. These exact bounds are upstream metadata, not independently verified provider-validator behavior.

Documentation-checked draft only; `terraform validate` and live apply were not run. No limits or identification settings were invented.
